OL,3,APalace in war of words with Earl
OL,4,ASpencer over claims in Diana book
OL,5,
OL,6,FBuckingham Palace is in a war of words
OL,7,Fwith Earl Spencer, brother of Diana,
OL,8,FPrincess of Wales, over a controversial
OL,9,Fmemoir about her life and death.
OL,11,FKing Charles III is accused of
OL,12,Finsensitively telling Earl Spencer, in
OL,13,Fthe wake of Princess Diana's death in
OL,14,F1997, that "we'll forget her soon
OL,15,Fenough", according to excerpts in the
OL,16,FDaily Mail.
OL,18,FBut the Palace has pushed back
OL,19,Funusually strongly, angered by the
OL,20,Fclaims and attempting to cast doubt on
OL,21,Fthem.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,163,160,200,105,0,100
